{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1020757-hurt-locker-drones","id":1020757,"title":"Hurt Locker: Drones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-21T19:18:20-08:00","id":1020757,"title":"Hurt Locker: Drones","content":"Some people requested more on drones. I couldn't fit anything of that scope into the book in the errata pass. And frankly, that'd be a whole bunch of words I couldn't hire a writer for. But, I wanted to give a little stop-gap to help your chronicles out a bit. So here you go. Rules for drones, including five barebones samples and a simple system for modifying them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-droning-on-and-on/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-droning-on-and-on/\" target=\"_blank\"> Hurt Locker: Droning On And On &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-droning-on-and-on/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/hurt-locker-droning-on-and-on/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:09:56-08:00","id":1020884,"title":"","content":"Fairly good, though the rules on secondary abilities and the limits on modifications are a bit confusing, yet. The limit on Size takes into account the sum of modifications? The mod to add Size counts itself? It adds to the final limit? If not, is there a mod to add to the limit? I'm not saying such limits have to exist, but it isn't clear if they do.<br /> <br /> Also, the main rule on Secondaries seems to state that the drone have its own pool, but the examples seem to imply it actually modify the character rolls. It isn't clear how it interacts to Specialty rules, if they're limited to specialties or benefit from them.<br /> <br /> I think it should be fairly conservative on Secondary abilities. A machine shouldn't have more than 2 dice to begin with by itself, and pools larger than 4 should be given only to highly specialized actions, or with delay on action to account for analysis of the situation. An attack drone that shoots by itself can get a fairly good pool to hit a head if given good hardware and software to do this, but its ability to shoot something that isn't a head, or impaired by being shoot on the head, should be poor to non-existent without time, and maybe outside help, to change parameters. On the same note, I think that an RC Ability Check should start with at least as much a penalty as the check to maneuver, probably worse, and limit the bonuses that can be added to it, unless the user get a way to actually transport its consciousness to the drone and adapt to the new body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","